{"reference":"Luke 2","book":"Luke","chapter":2,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Questions About the Enrollment","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Luke’s reference to an enrollment associated with Quirinius raises an unresolved chronological question. Quirinius’s documented Syrian governorship and census belong to 6 CE, while Luke also connects Jesus’ birth with Herod’s era. Proposed explanations exist, but the difficulty remains disputed rather than settled.","verse_refs":["Luke 2:1-5","Luke 2:1-52","Luke 2:14"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_luke_002_2b13a4d906e0d7cb4def5012"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"language_literary","title":"Wording and Design","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The wording of the angels’ praise in verse 14 has a well-known textual and grammatical variation. It is commonly translated either as peace among people of God’s favor, or as goodwill toward people; a translation should make the issue visible rather than treating one wording as unquestioned.\n\nLuke 1–2 also places John and Jesus in deliberately paired scenes: announcements, births, songs, Spirit-filled speech, temple episodes, and notices of growth. This literary pattern helps readers see Luke 2 as part of a larger, carefully shaped opening narrative.","verse_refs":["Luke 2:1-5","Luke 2:1-52","Luke 2:14"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_luke_002_2b13a4d906e0d7cb4def5012"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"why_it_matters","title":"Festival Travel and the Temple","blocks":[{"id":"block_3","text":"The chapter begins with travel for registration and closes with the family’s annual Passover journey to Jerusalem. Festival travel involved more than a private trip: the Gospel portrayals connect it with lodging, offerings, exchange, animal sales, crowds, teaching, and conflict in the temple precincts. This wider setting helps place Jesus’ presence among the teachers within the practical and public life gathered around a festival.","verse_refs":["Luke 2:1-7","Luke 2:41-52"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_luke_002_0aa86e627f021c79ff2b37c9"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}